The Conditional Test.

Romeo, a young man.
Juliet, a young woman.

Act I: Conditionals.
Scene I: All forms.

[Enter Romeo and Juliet]

Juliet:
Am I as good as you?
Am I as bad as you?
Am I better than you?
Am I worse than you?
Am I not as good as you?
Am I not better than you?
Am I not worse than you?
Is Romeo as good as Juliet?
Is Juliet better than Romeo?

Romeo:
If so, let us proceed to scene I.
If not, let us proceed to scene I.
Let us proceed to scene II.
Let us return to act I.

[Exeunt]
